# CH01 — The Orders We Carry. Brackenford and Crown Quarry.
# Key scenes SC01/SC02 use the authored dialogue from docs/17; connective dialogue is newly written.

@scene OPENING once
music M010
say narr | Brackenford Halt. The morning train from Veyr, three hours late.
still ST00_opening
say inspector | Captain Raven. The quarry gate is up the north road. The regulator report is due by the evening bell.
say dain | Understood.
say inspector | Whatever the crew tells you, Captain, production is not your department.
move inspector up
hide inspector
objective | Report to Crown Quarry's gate, north of town.
@end

@scene T01_INSPECTOR
say inspector | The gate is north. I will meet you there, Captain.
@end

@scene T01_WORKER_LIST
if flag:sc00_done again
say worker | I'm not getting on that train. Not till someone checks the list.
say dain | What list?
say worker | Seven of ours went down at dawn. None came up. Mara's gone to the gate to count them herself.
say worker | You're ministry.
say dain | Crown's Executioner. Raven.
say worker | The badge means they sent you.
say dain | It means I can open a gate.
say worker | Then open it. Mara's up there already, arguing with a man who thinks people are a schedule.
set sc00_done
objective worker | Go north to the quarry gate. Mara is counting her crew.
end
label again
say worker | Seven names. Mara has them. Go.
@end

@scene T01_KEEPER
say keeper | Tonics, ether, a few blades. Everyone's wages are three months late, so I write it in the book.
say keeper | You're not on the book, Captain. You pay.
shop SHOP_T01
@end

@scene T01_CHILD
say child | Mum says the quarry sings at night. I've heard it. It's not singing. It's more like a door creaking.
@end

@scene T01_FARMER
say farmer | Rails through my beans, again. The ministry paid for the track, not the beans.
say farmer | River road south goes to Veyr. Two days on foot if the bridge holds.
@end

@scene T01_ELDER
say elder | Forty years I cut stone up there. Heartglass was just a bad seam, then. Red and warm.
say elder | Nobody called it fuel till the regulators came. Now it hums at night and they call that pressure.
rumor | An old quarryman says the heartglass started humming after the regulators arrived.
@end

@scene T01_LAUNDRESS
say narr | Shirts on the line, each with a number stitched at the collar.
say worker | Shift numbers. I stitch the names on the inside where the foreman can't see.
@end

@scene T01_GUARD
say guard | Captain. Quiet post, this. Rats in the drains, a few angry wives. The quarry does its own policing.
@end

@scene T01_CARTMAN
say worker | Lunch carts go up at noon. Nobody's eaten today. The crew's still under.
@end

@scene T01_BAKER
say baker | Shared oven. Every house brings its dough, every house takes its loaf. Mara's crew gets theirs first when they come up.
say baker | When. Not if.
@end

@scene T01_BAKERY_WORKER
say worker | They docked us for the flooded lift. Docked us for the water.
@end

@scene T01_BAKERY_CHILD
say child | Is my dad one of the seven? His name's Tobbe. He's got a bad knee.
@end

@scene T01_BUNK_INN
say elder | Bunkhouse beds. Twenty-five crowns a head, and the stove is free.
inn
@end

@scene T01_SLEEPER
say worker | Night shift. Go away. Unless it's about the lift. Is it about the lift?
@end

@scene T01_MARA_MOTHER
say elder | Mara's out counting again. She counts everyone. Her father was never counted, so she counts.
@end

@scene T01_TALLY
say clerk | I keep the town's own tally. Injuries, deaths, who's owed. The ministry keeps a different one.
say clerk | They don't match. They never have.
@end

@scene T01_MARA_AFTER
say mara | Seven came up. Tonight I'll count them twice.
say mara | You've got a long walk to Veyr, Captain. Don't let them make you into a report.
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Gatehouse
@scene D01_MARA_GATE
say mara | The lift is filling. Talk to the inspector if you want permission. I'm not waiting for it.
@end

@scene D01_INSPECTOR
if flag:sc01_done after
say inspector | Captain, the regulator is behind the heartglass face. Everything else is a distraction.
end
label after
say inspector | You are exceeding your orders, Captain. I will be writing this down.
@end

@scene D01_GATE_GUARD
say guard | The drains back up into the yard. Pump handles by the alcoves clear them. Old kit, but it works.
@end

@scene D01_SC01 once
face player up
music M020
say mara | The lift is filling. My people are below it.
still ST01_quarry
say inspector | Production cannot stop on an unverified report.
say dain | How many?
say mara | Seven. I have their names.
say inspector | Captain, the inspection is about the regulator.
say dain | Then the regulator can wait.
say mara | It never has before.
say dain | Show me the lift.
say mara | Hesk. Anni. Tobbe. Marit. Joss. Wren. Old Cale. Say them back to me when you find them.
say mara | The gallery's below the gate. The loft pumps can clear the spur, if anyone still knows how to run them.
set sc01_done
setvar workers 0
objective mara | Find Mara's seven workers below Crown Quarry, then get them out.
say guard | Rats in the gate drains again, Captain. Mind your feet.
battle D01_T noflee
say narr | Attack strikes with your weapon. Defend halves the next blow until you act again.
@end

@scene D01_PUMP0
if flag:d01_pump0 done
say narr | An old hand pump. The alcove behind it is flooded to the knee.
choice | Work the pump handle -> pump | Leave it -> leave
label pump
sfx FX010
set d01_pump0
say narr | The handle groans. Water sucks away through the grate, and the alcove floor shows again.
end
label done
say narr | The alcove is drained.
end
label leave
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Lunch Gallery
@scene D01_TESSA_GUARD
say guard | She stays put, Captain. Detained for relay tampering.
@end

@scene D01_TESSA once
say tessa | Don't touch anything. If I let go of this, the gallery lamps die and the second pump seizes.
say tessa | It's like holding a door shut against a crowd, using a teaspoon.
say dain | Who detained you?
say tessa | The ministry. For telling them the relay was overloaded. Which it was. Which I proved by overloading it.
say tessa determined | Which, yes, was a mistake.
say dain | Can you run a pump?
say tessa | I can hold one handle open. Not both. Nobody can do both.
say dain | Then hold one. Guard - she comes with me. My order.
say guard | On your badge, Captain.
say tessa | Your badge. Fine. I'll owe it a thank-you note.
set d01_tessa_circuit
join C02
say narr | Morwen's Magic spends MP. Ember Lance burns what fire hurts; flasks work for anyone and cost no MP.
@end

@scene D01_LIST once
say narr | Under a lunch pail, a shift sheet. Seven names, each ticked at dawn. None ticked since.
doc Shift_Sheet | Lower gallery, dawn shift. Hesk - pump crew. Anni - rail. Tobbe - rail (knee). Marit - face. Joss - face. Wren - carrier. Old Cale - lamps. Signed out: none.
key K_WORKER_LIST
if party:C02 tessa
end
label tessa
say tessa | Somebody wrote 'production units: 7' in the margin. Somebody else crossed it out and wrote the names back.
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Workers (all recoverable, any order)
@scene D01_W1 once
say worker | You're not the ministry. The ministry doesn't come down here.
say dain | Mara sent me. Name?
say worker | Hesk. Pump crew. The pump crew with no pump.
say dain | Hesk. Go up the gallery to the gate. Mara is counting.
set d01_w1
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W2 once
say worker | I can't swim and the island got smaller.
say dain | Walk where the water's shallow. It's marked.
say worker | Anni. Rail crew. Tell Mara I didn't leave the others. The water left me.
set d01_w2
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W3 once
say worker | My knee went when the rail jumped. I've been sitting here counting drips.
say dain | Tobbe?
say worker | How do you know?
say dain | Your son asked. The bakery.
say worker | Oh. Then I'd better walk.
set d01_w3
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W4 once
say worker | Marit. Face crew. We heard the heartglass knock. Like knuckles on a door.
say worker | The foreman said pressure. It knocked in threes.
set d01_w4
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W5 once
say worker | Joss. I stayed with the lift cable so nobody would open it with Wren's cousins aboard.
say dain | The lift gate stays shut.
say worker | Good. Say that to anyone who has a lever.
set d01_w5
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W6 once
say worker | Wren. Carrier. I was bringing water to the face when the lamps went strange.
say worker | The big machine says things. Not words. Near words.
set d01_w6
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_W7 once
say worker | Old Cale. Lamps. Forty years. Lamps don't lie, and every one of them is leaning toward that face.
say dain | Come up to the lift, Cale.
set d01_w7
addvar workers 1
say narr | Workers found: {v:workers} of 7.
@end

@scene D01_RESCUED
say worker | We wait for the rest. Mara's rule.
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Pump Loft
@scene D01_PUMP1
if flag:d01_drained done
if flag:d01_p2 pull
say narr | A pump handle, linked by a long rod to its twin across the loft.
if party:C02 ask
say narr | The handle moves, but water rushes back through the other valve. It needs two people.
end
label ask
choice | Ask Morwen to hold this handle -> hold | Pull it alone -> alone
label hold
set d01_p1
unset d01_p2
say tessa | Holding. Go pull the other one before my arms remember they're arms.
end
label alone
sfx FX010
say narr | The handle moves, but the water rushes back through the other valve.
end
label pull
call D01_DRAIN
end
label done
say narr | The channel is drained.
@end

@scene D01_PUMP2
if flag:d01_drained done
if flag:d01_p1 pull
say narr | A pump handle, linked by a long rod to its twin across the loft.
if party:C02 ask
say narr | The handle moves, but water rushes back through the other valve. It needs two people.
end
label ask
choice | Ask Morwen to hold this handle -> hold | Pull it alone -> alone
label hold
set d01_p2
unset d01_p1
say tessa | Holding. Other side. Quickly, please.
end
label alone
sfx FX010
say narr | The handle moves, but the water rushes back through the other valve.
end
label pull
call D01_DRAIN
end
label done
say narr | The channel is drained.
@end

@scene D01_DRAIN
sfx FX010
shake 0.4
say narr | Both pumps turn together. The channel north of the loft drains into the old sump.
set d01_drained
unset d01_p1
unset d01_p2
say tessa | One crew holds, the other pulls. That's the whole secret. Someone built it so nobody could do it alone.
say dain | The ore cart is still on the track north. The brake is by the lift.
@end

@scene D01_BRAKE
if flag:d01_brake done
if flag:d01_drained ok
say narr | The track north is under water. Releasing the cart now would sink it in the channel.
end
label ok
sfx FX010
set d01_brake
say narr | The rail brake releases. The ore cart rolls north, clear of the passage, and thumps into the buffer.
end
label done
say narr | The brake is released.
@end

@scene D01_LIFTLEVER
say narr | The lift gate lever. Through the grille, the lift cage hangs with three people aboard.
say dain | Not that one.
@end

@scene D01_LOFTGATE
if flag:d01_loftgate done
sfx FX009
set d01_loftgate
say narr | The service latch lifts. The lunch gallery is just below: a shorter way back.
end
label done
say narr | The service gate is open.
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Heartglass Face
@scene D01_SC02 once
music silence
show inspector 20 28 up inspector
say narr | The heartglass face fills the chamber. Something in it pulses, slow and warm.
say tessa | That pulse is answering the pump.
say dain | Pressure does that.
say tessa concern | Not with your name.
wait 0.4
say ilyr | Little ember.
say dain | Who said that?
say tessa | You heard it too.
say inspector | Resonance artifact. Restart the line.
say dain | No.
wait 0.6
say narr | The extractor light dims rather than flares. Then its red gauge begins to climb.
hide inspector
battle B01 noflee
set b01_done
music M020
say narr | The Warden shudders and goes still. Its arm locks above the occupied lift - disconnected, not destroyed.
say ilyr | That is not a stone.
say tessa | Raven. You heard that.
say dain | I heard it.
objective | Get the workers out through the Lift Yard, east of the face.
xp 60
@end

# ------------------------------------------------------------------ Lift Yard
@scene D01_YARD_ARRIVE once
say mara | You broke the Warden. The yard lift runs on counterweight now. We can take them up.
call D01_MARA_YARD
@end

@scene D01_MARA_YARD
if var:workers>=7 depart
say mara | I count {v:workers}. Seven went down. We wait.
say mara | Hesk, Anni, Tobbe, Marit, Joss, Wren, Old Cale. Whoever's missing is still below.
end
label depart
call D01_DEPART
@end

@scene D01_DEPART once
say mara | Hesk. Anni. Tobbe. Marit. Joss. Wren. Old Cale.
say mara | All seven.
show inspector 4 8 right inspector
say inspector | Captain. The line restarts at noon. The heartglass face is intact, which is the one mercy in this.
say dain | It is not a stone.
say inspector | I beg your pardon?
say dain | I will not order this line restarted.
say inspector | Then you will explain that refusal to the ministry in Veyr. In person.
say inspector | And the apprentice returns to custody. With the heartglass samples, which are worth more than -
say tessa | Than seven names? Your ledger says so.
say tessa determined | I'm taking the list. You can keep the rocks.
say mara | Up we go. Everyone holds the rail. Nobody is last.
fade out 0.6
chapter CH01
unset d01_p1
warp T01_PLATFORM from_quarry down
fade in 0.6
say narr | Evening. The lift yard is quiet. The quarry does not sing.
call V01_PACT
say tessa | They'll arrest you in Veyr.
say dain | Probably.
say tessa | I'm coming anyway. Somebody has to explain relays to a courtroom.
objective inspector | Report to the ministry in Veyr, south across the river.
discover L_T02
level_floor 4
@end

@scene V01_PACT once
say narr | A small moth of ember light has followed Raven up from the quarry. It settles on his gauntlet.
say ilyr | It came out of the dimmed machine. It asks to travel. It does not ask to be carried.
say dain | Then it walks with us. Or flies.
say narr | The Ember Moth offers a small pact: it will help when called, and leave when it chooses.
vestige V01
say narr | (Link a Vestige to a party member from Vestiges in the menu. Summons spend 100 Concord.)
@end
